{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CkwR8X3uXfAHMYpczjW91r","type":"tool_result","content":"total 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff      128 Nov 21 13:21 .\ndrwx------@ 33222 brenn  staff  1063104 Nov 21 13:21 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    14 brenn  staff      448 Oct  2 03:50 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff     5504 Nov 21 13:21 sheet.md\n# Independent coverage discovery: A03 — Content-derived type identity\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Compute the agent-type-id as a hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration. The model part includes checkpoint and fine-tune or adapter references where they apply. Keep the list of inputs (the manifest) and the hashing steps. Check that changing any input changes the ID, and that the same manifest gives the same ID.\n**N/A condition:** never\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\nomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\ninput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\nSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\ncoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\nby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\njust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n\nSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## A03.1\n\n**Check:** The agent-type-id is a hash over a manifest that includes the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the code or CI step that computes `agent.type.id` (search `sha256`, `hashlib`, `createHash`, `type_id`). 2) List its inputs. 3) Check each is there: container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, configuration. 4) Answer no if the ID is a label, version string, or git tag, or any input is missing.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A03.2\n\n**Check:** The hash covers every file that defines the prompt, tools, and configuration, with no file or directory skipped or excluded.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the function that lists files to hash. 2) Write down every filter it applies: hidden files, names starting with '_' or '__', extensions, ignore lists, glob patterns. 3) For each filter, check whether a file that defines tools, prompts, or config would be skipped (for example `__init__.py`, `index.ts`, `.env`, `config/*.local.*`). 4) Answer no if any such file is skipped.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A03.3\n\n**Check:** The model input is a pinned version or snapshot (plus checkpoint and adapter references where used), not an alias and not the app's release number.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the model ID that goes into the manifest or hash. 2) Follow env vars and config to the final value, including defaults such as `getenv('MODEL', ...)`. 3) Answer no if it is an alias (`-latest`, no date or version), falls back to one when unset, or is the app release number. Also no if adapters or checkpoints are used but left out.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A03.4\n\n**Check:** The manifest is put in a fixed, documented order before hashing, so the same manifest always gives the same ID.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the serialization step before hashing. 2) Check for a fixed order: sorted keys (`sort_keys=True`), sorted file lists, fixed encoding and line endings. 3) Check file lists are not taken straight from directory listing or map iteration order. 4) Answer no if any unsorted dict, map, or filesystem order reaches the hash.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## A03.5\n\n**Check:** Secret values are not placed in the hashed manifest in a form that exposes them.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) List every value fed into the manifest or hash. 2) Check whether any are secrets: API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, `.env` contents. 3) Answer no if a secret value is written in plain text to the stored manifest, or the whole environment is dumped into it.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to A03.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"A03\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"A03.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the re